      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That analogy of the filling room is powerful, and it speaks to a deep sense of entrapment. When the external pressures are so absolute, the focus shifts from fixing the external problems to finding a way to create internal space. If the room itself can't be left, perhaps the goal isn't to stop the water, but to find a way to make the pressure of the water feel less overwhelming in the moment.",
      "source": "target",
